    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nIntroduced address normalization for owner creation, defined in one place and applied consistently everywhere addresses are stored or compared.\n\n**New: `AddressNormalizer`** (`rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`) \u2014 mirrors the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` pattern. `normalize(address)`:\n- trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces,\n- upper-cases,\n- expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`,\n- returns `\"\"` for a `null`/all-whitespace address.\n\n**`BuildOwner`** \u2014 normalizes the address up front, so:\n- the required-field check now flags `address` as missing when it's blank *after* normalization (fixing the `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize` 400 case),\n- the normalized form is written back onto the request (`request.setAddress(...)`) before mapping, so it's what gets stored and returned.\n\n**`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 household duplicate detection and the derived shared `householdId` now compare `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` of both the new and each existing owner's address, so `\"12 main st\"` and `\"12 MAIN STREET\"` are treated as the same household.\n\n## Verification\n- The 3 new tests in `AcceptanceTest` (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) pass.\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne behavioral note worth flagging: since `householdId` is derived from the normalized last name + address, any household ids computed for the same address under the old (lowercase, un-expanded) form would now hash differently \u2014 expected given the spec's requirement that the shared household id use the normalized form.",
